<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lazic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">541–562</span> · Also known as Colchidian War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lazic War was fought from 541 to 562 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> for control of Lazica, the kingdom of the Lazi on the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast. Invited by King Gubazes II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a> took the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petra">Petra</a>, but Byzantine and Lazic forces retook it in 551 and held most of the country. The Fifty-Year Peace of 562 left Lazica to Byzantium in return for annual payments to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>.</p></div>
